{"id":"mahabharata-6-061","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":61,"title":"एकषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 61 · Duryodhana's fear and Bhishma's hymn to Narayana","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra is amazed at the Pandavas' deeds and fears for his sons. Duryodhana questions Bhishma, who begins the ancient praise in which the gods and sages hymn Narayana.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರ ಸಾಹಸ ಕಂಡು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಬೆರಗಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಪ್ರಶ್ನಿಸಲು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ದೇವ-ಋಷಿಗಳು ನಾರಾಯಣನನ್ನು ಸ್ತುತಿಸಿದ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ ಸ್ತೋತ್ರವನ್ನು ಆರಂಭಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पाण्डवों के कर्म सुनकर धृतराष्ट्र चकित होते हैं। दुर्योधन भीष्म से प्रश्न करता है और भीष्म देवताओं तथा ऋषियों द्वारा नारायण की प्राचीन स्तुति आरम्भ करते हैं।","te":"పాండవుల పరాక్రమం విని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు ఆశ్చర్యపోతాడు. దుర్యోధనుడు భీష్ముని ప్రశ్నించగా భీష్ముడు దేవతలు, ఋషులు నారాయణుని స్తుతించిన ప్రాచీన స్తోత్రాన్ని మొదలుపెడతాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவரின் செயல்களைக் கேட்டுத் த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் வியக்கிறான். துரியோதனன் பீஷ்மரை வினவ, பீஷ்மர் தேவரும் முனிவரும் நாராயணனைப் போற்றிய பழைய துதியைத் தொடங்குகிறார்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവരുടെ പ്രവൃത്തികളിൽ വിസ്മയിക്കുന്ന ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ മക്കളെക്കുറിച്ച് ഭയപ്പെടുന്നു. ദുര്യോധനൻ ഭീഷ്മരോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു; ദേവന്മാരും ഋഷിമാരും നാരായണനെ സ്തുതിക്കുന്ന പുരാതന സ്തോത്രം ഭീഷ്മർ ആരംഭിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.61; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भयं मे सुमहज्जातं विस्मयश्चैव संजय ।\nश्रुत्वा पाण्डुकुमाराणां कर्म देवैः सुदुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great fear and wonder have come over me, Sanjaya, hearing of the deeds of the Pandu princes, so hard for even gods to do."}},{"n":2,"text":"पुत्राणां च पराभवं श्रुत्वा संजय सर्वशः ।\nचिन्ता मे महती सूत भविष्यति कथं त्विति ॥","meaning":{"en":"And hearing of my sons' defeat on every side, Sanjaya, a great anxiety grips me, charioteer: how will it all turn out?"}},{"n":3,"text":"ध्रुवं विदुरवाक्यानि धक्ष्यन्ति हृदयं मम ।\nयथा हि दृश्यते सर्वं दैवयोगेन संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely Vidura's words will burn my heart, since everything is seen to happen as by the working of fate, Sanjaya."}},{"n":4,"text":"यत्र भीष्ममुखाञ्शूरानस्त्रज्ञान्योधसत्तमान् ।\nपाण्डवानामनीकानि योधयन्ति प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the Pandava armies are fighting warriors who strike hard, headed by Bhishma, the best of fighters, skilled in weapons."}},{"n":5,"text":"केनावध्या महात्मानः पाण्डुपुत्रा महाबलाः ।\nकेन दत्तवरास्तात किं वा ज्ञानं विदन्ति ते ।\nयेन क्षयं न गच्छन्ति दिवि तारागणा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"By what are the mighty sons of Pandu unslayable? Who gave them boons, my dear? Or what knowledge do they have, that they do not perish, like the stars in the sky?"}},{"n":6,"text":"पुनः पुनर्न मृष्यामि हतं सैन्यं स्म पाण्डवैः ।\nमय्येव दण्डः पतति दैवात्परमदारुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again and again I cannot bear that my army is struck by the Pandavas; the fearful rod of punishment falls on me alone, by fate."}},{"n":7,"text":"यथावध्याः पाण्डुसुता यथा वध्याश्च मे सुताः ।\nएतन्मे सर्वमाचक्ष्व यथातत्त्वेन संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me all as it truly is, Sanjaya: why the sons of Pandu cannot be killed and why my sons can."}},{"n":8,"text":"न हि पारं प्रपश्यामि दुःखस्यास्य कथंचन ।\nसमुद्रस्येव महतो भुजाभ्यां प्रतरन्नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see no way to the far shore of this grief, like a man trying to swim across a great ocean with his arms."}},{"n":9,"text":"पुत्राणां व्यसनं मन्ये ध्रुवं प्राप्तं सुदारुणम् ।\nघातयिष्यति मे पुत्रान्सर्वान्भीमो न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think a terrible disaster has surely come upon my sons; Bhima will have all my sons killed, without doubt."}},{"n":10,"text":"न हि पश्यामि तं वीरं यो मे रक्षेत्सुतान्रणे ।\nध्रुवं विनाशः समरे पुत्राणां मम संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not see any hero who could guard my sons in battle. Surely my sons will perish in the war, Sanjaya."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्मान्मे कारणं सूत युक्तिं चैव विशेषतः ।\nपृच्छतोऽद्य यथातत्त्वं सर्वमाख्यातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, charioteer, as I ask you, you should tell me the cause and the reasoning, above all, exactly and in full."}},{"n":12,"text":"दुर्योधनोऽपि यच्चक्रे दृष्ट्वा स्वान्विमुखान्रणे ।\nभीष्मद्रोणौ कृपश्चैव सौबलेयो जयद्रथः ।\nद्रौणिर्वापि महेष्वासो विकर्णो वा महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me too what Duryodhana did when he saw his men turn their backs in battle, and what Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, Shakuni's son, Jayadratha, Drona's son the great archer, or mighty Vikarna did."}},{"n":13,"text":"निश्चयो वापि कस्तेषां तदा ह्यासीन्महात्मनाम् ।\nविमुखेषु महाप्राज्ञ मम पुत्रेषु संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"What was the decision of those great-souled men then, wise Sanjaya, when my sons had turned away?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"शृणु राजन्नवहितः श्रुत्वा चैवावधारय ।\nनैव मन्त्रकृतं किंचिन्नैव मायां तथाविधाम् ।\nन वै विभीषिकां कांचिद्राजन्कुर्वन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen carefully, king, and having heard, take it to heart. The Pandavas use no spell, no illusion of that sort, and no kind of terrifying trick."}},{"n":15,"text":"युध्यन्ति ते यथान्यायं शक्तिमन्तश्च संयुगे ।\nधर्मेण सर्वकार्याणि कीर्तितानीति भारत ।\nआरभन्ते सदा पार्थाः प्रार्थयाना महद्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They fight rightly and with all their strength in battle. All their undertakings, Bharata, are done by dharma, they say. The sons of Pritha always begin, seeking great glory."}},{"n":16,"text":"न ते युद्धान्निवर्तन्ते धर्मोपेता महाबलाः ।\nश्रिया परमया युक्ता यतो धर्मस्ततो जयः ।\nतेनावध्या रणे पार्था जययुक्ताश्च पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those mighty men of dharma do not turn back from battle, and are joined with the highest fortune. Where dharma is, there is victory. So the Parthas are unslayable in battle and victorious, king."}},{"n":17,"text":"तव पुत्रा दुरात्मानः पापेष्वभिरताः सदा ।\nनिष्ठुरा हीनकर्माणस्तेन हीयन्ति संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your wicked sons are always devoted to sinful things, cruel and base in their conduct; so they are losing in battle."}},{"n":18,"text":"सुबहूनि नृशंसानि पुत्रैस्तव जनेश्वर ।\nनिकृतानीह पाण्डूनां नीचैरिव यथा नरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons, lord of men, have done very many cruel wrongs to the sons of Pandu, as base men might do."}},{"n":19,"text":"सर्वं च तदनादृत्य पुत्राणां तव किल्बिषम् ।\nसापह्नवाः सदैवासन्पाण्डवाः पाण्डुपूर्वज ।\nन चैनान्बहु मन्यन्ते पुत्रास्तव विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ignoring all that guilt of your sons, the Pandavas, elder kinsmen of Pandu's line, were always put upon with deceit; and your sons do not hold them in much regard, lord of the people."}},{"n":20,"text":"तस्य पापस्य सततं क्रियमाणस्य कर्मणः ।\nसंप्राप्तं सुमहद्घोरं फलं किंपाकसंनिभम् ।\nस तद्भुङ्क्ष्व महाराज सपुत्रः ससुहृज्जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From that sin, committed continually, a very great and terrible fruit, like the kimpaka fruit, has now come. Eat it, great king, with your sons and friends."}},{"n":21,"text":"नावबुध्यसि यद्राजन्वार्यमाणः सुहृज्जनैः ।\nविदुरेणाथ भीष्मेण द्रोणेन च महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"You do not understand, king, though you were warned by your friends, by Vidura, by Bhishma and by the great-souled Drona."}},{"n":22,"text":"तथा मया चाप्यसकृद्वार्यमाणो न गृह्णसि ।\nवाक्यं हितं च पथ्यं च मर्त्यः पथ्यमिवौषधम् ।\nपुत्राणां मतमास्थाय जितान्मन्यसि पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And though I too warned you again and again, you do not accept it, as a sick man does not accept good medicine, and you accept your sons' counsel and think the Pandavas are already beaten."}},{"n":23,"text":"शृणु भूयो यथातत्त्वं यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ।\nकारणं भरतश्रेष्ठ पाण्डवानां जयं प्रति ।\nतत्तेऽहं कथयिष्यामि यथाश्रुतमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear again, truly, what you ask me, best of the Bharatas, the reason for the Pandavas' victory. I will tell you, scourge of foes, as I heard it."}},{"n":24,"text":"दुर्योधनेन संपृष्ट एतमर्थं पितामहः ।\nदृष्ट्वा भ्रातॄन्रणे सर्वान्निर्जितान्सुमहारथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Duryodhana put this very question to the grandsire, having seen all his brothers and great chariot-warriors beaten in the battle,"}},{"n":25,"text":"शोकसंमूढहृदयो निशाकाले स्म कौरवः ।\nपितामहं महाप्राज्ञं विनयेनोपगम्य ह ।\nयदब्रवीत्सुतस्तेऽसौ तन्मे शृणु जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"his heart bewildered with grief, the Kaurava went at night, humbly, to the wise grandsire. Hear from me, lord of men, what your son said."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"त्वं च द्रोणश्च शल्यश्च कृपो द्रौणिस्तथैव च ।\nकृतवर्मा च हार्दिक्यः काम्बोजश्च सुदक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You and Drona, Shalya, Kripa and Drona's son, Kritavarma, the Hardikya, and Sudakshina of the Kambojas,"}},{"n":27,"text":"भूरिश्रवा विकर्णश्च भगदत्तश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nमहारथाः समाख्याताः कुलपुत्रास्तनुत्यजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Vikarna, and the mighty Bhagadatta are all declared great chariot-warriors, of good families, ready to give up their lives."}},{"n":28,"text":"त्रयाणामपि लोकानां पर्याप्ता इति मे मतिः ।\nपाण्डवानां समस्ताश्च न तिष्ठन्ति पराक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In my opinion you are enough for all three worlds, and all the Pandavas together do not stand against your prowess."}},{"n":29,"text":"तत्र मे संशयो जातस्तन्ममाचक्ष्व पृच्छतः ।\nयं समाश्रित्य कौन्तेया जयन्त्यस्मान्पदे पदे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet a doubt has arisen in me, and I ask you to tell me: relying on whom do the sons of Kunti defeat us at every step?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"शृणु राजन्वचो मह्यं यत्त्वां वक्ष्यामि कौरव ।\nबहुशश्च ममोक्तोऽसि न च मे तत्त्वया कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen, king, to the words I will speak to you, Kaurava. I have spoken to you many times, but you have not acted on what I said."}},{"n":31,"text":"क्रियतां पाण्डवैः सार्धं शमो भरतसत्तम ।\nएतत्क्षममहं मन्ये पृथिव्यास्तव चाभिभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Make peace with the Pandavas, best of the Bharatas. That, I think, is right for the earth and for you, master."}},{"n":32,"text":"भुञ्जेमां पृथिवीं राजन्भ्रातृभिः सहितः सुखी ।\nदुर्हृदस्तापयन्सर्वान्नन्दयंश्चापि बान्धवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enjoy this earth, king, happily with your brothers, giving pain to ill-wishers and delighting your kinsmen."}},{"n":33,"text":"न च मे क्रोशतस्तात श्रुतवानसि वै पुरा ।\nतदिदं समनुप्राप्तं यत्पाण्डूनवमन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"My dear, you did not listen to me before when I cried out; and this has now come about because you despise the Pandavas."}},{"n":34,"text":"यश्च हेतुरवध्यत्वे तेषामक्लिष्टकर्मणाम् ।\nतं शृणुष्व महाराज मम कीर्तयतः प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear, great king, from me as I tell it, the cause of their being unslayable, those whose deeds are free of blemish."}},{"n":35,"text":"नास्ति लोकेषु तद्भूतं भविता नो भविष्यति ।\nयो जयेत्पाण्डवान्संख्ये पालिताञ्शार्ङ्गधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no being in the worlds, nor has there been, nor will there be, who could defeat in battle the Pandavas protected by the wielder of the Sharnga bow."}},{"n":36,"text":"यत्तु मे कथितं तात मुनिभिर्भावितात्मभिः ।\nपुराणगीतं धर्मज्ञ तच्छृणुष्व यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But hear, my dear who know dharma, what sages of purified souls told me, sung in ancient times, just as it was."}},{"n":37,"text":"पुरा किल सुराः सर्वे ऋषयश्च समागताः ।\nपितामहमुपासेदुः पर्वते गन्धमादने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, it is said, all the gods and sages came together and attended the grandfather on Mount Gandhamadana."}},{"n":38,"text":"मध्ये तेषां समासीनः प्रजापतिरपश्यत ।\nविमानं जाज्वलद्भासा स्थितं प्रवरमम्बरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seated in their midst, the lord of creatures saw a supreme celestial car, blazing with light, standing in the sky."}},{"n":39,"text":"ध्यानेनावेद्य तं ब्रह्मा कृत्वा च नियतोऽञ्जलिम् ।\nनमश्चकार हृष्टात्मा परमं परमेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma, knowing him through meditation, joined his palms with self-control and, glad in heart, bowed to the supreme Lord of lords."}},{"n":40,"text":"ऋषयस्त्वथ देवाश्च दृष्ट्वा ब्रह्माणमुत्थितम् ।\nस्थिताः प्राञ्जलयः सर्वे पश्यन्तो महदद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the sages and gods saw Brahma stand up, they all stood with joined palms, watching that great marvel."}},{"n":41,"text":"यथावच्च तमभ्यर्च्य ब्रह्मा ब्रह्मविदां वरः ।\nजगाद जगतः स्रष्टा परं परमधर्मवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having duly worshipped him, Brahma, best of Brahma-knowers, creator of the world, knower of the highest dharma, spoke to the Supreme:"}},{"n":42,"text":"विश्वावसुर्विश्वमूर्तिर्विश्वेशो\nविष्वक्सेनो विश्वकर्मा वशी च ।\nविश्वेश्वरो वासुदेवोऽसि तस्मा-\nद्योगात्मानं दैवतं त्वामुपैमि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are Vishvavasu, of all forms, lord of all, Vishvaksena, maker of all, self-controlled, Lord of the universe, Vasudeva. Therefore I come to you, the god who is the self of yoga."}},{"n":43,"text":"जय विश्व महादेव जय लोकहिते रत ।\nजय योगीश्वर विभो जय योगपरावर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory to you, All, great god! Victory, you who delight in the good of the worlds! Victory, lord of yogis, all-pervading! Victory, supreme above yoga!"}},{"n":44,"text":"पद्मगर्भ विशालाक्ष जय लोकेश्वरेश्वर ।\nभूतभव्यभवन्नाथ जय सौम्यात्मजात्मज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-womb, wide-eyed one, victory, lord of the lords of the world! Lord of what was, is and will be, victory, gentle self, self of the self-born!"}},{"n":45,"text":"असंख्येयगुणाजेय जय सर्वपरायण ।\nनारायण सुदुष्पार जय शार्ङ्गधनुर्धर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of countless virtues, unconquerable, victory, refuge of all! Narayana, hard to fathom, victory, bearer of the Sharnga bow!"}},{"n":46,"text":"सर्वगुह्यगुणोपेत विश्वमूर्ते निरामय ।\nविश्वेश्वर महाबाहो जय लोकार्थतत्पर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Possessed of all secret qualities, of all forms, free from ill, Lord of all, mighty-armed, victory, intent on the world's good!"}},{"n":47,"text":"महोरग वराहाद्य हरिकेश विभो जय ।\nहरिवास विशामीश विश्वावासामिताव्यय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great serpent, Boar and first of all, Harikesha, all-pervading one, victory! Dwelling of Hari, master of beings, home of the world, immeasurable and imperishable!"}},{"n":48,"text":"व्यक्ताव्यक्तामितस्थान नियतेन्द्रिय सेन्द्रिय ।\nअसंख्येयात्मभावज्ञ जय गम्भीर कामद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Manifest and unmanifest, of measureless station, controlled in senses and master of the senses, knower of countless states of being, victory, profound giver of desires!"}},{"n":49,"text":"अनन्त विदितप्रज्ञ नित्यं भूतविभावन ।\nकृतकार्य कृतप्रज्ञ धर्मज्ञ विजयाजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Endless, of known wisdom, forever the source of beings' becoming, whose work is done and wisdom accomplished, knower of dharma, victory and defeat!"}},{"n":50,"text":"गुह्यात्मन्सर्वभूतात्मन्स्फुटसंभूतसंभव ।\nभूतार्थतत्त्व लोकेश जय भूतविभावन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hidden self, self of all beings, born of clear origin, truth of the meaning of beings, lord of the world, victory, source of beings!"}},{"n":51,"text":"आत्मयोने महाभाग कल्पसंक्षेपतत्पर ।\nउद्भावन मनोद्भाव जय ब्रह्मजनप्रिय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Self-born, greatly blessed, intent on drawing in the cycle of ages, creator, mind-born, victory, beloved of the people of Brahma!"}},{"n":52,"text":"निसर्गसर्गाभिरत कामेश परमेश्वर ।\nअमृतोद्भव सद्भाव युगाग्ने विजयप्रद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Delighting in natural creation, lord of desire, supreme Lord, born of the nectar, true being, giver of victory at the end of the yuga!"}},{"n":53,"text":"प्रजापतिपते देव पद्मनाभ महाबल ।\nआत्मभूत महाभूत कर्मात्मञ्जय कर्मद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the lords of creatures, god, lotus-navel, of great strength, who has become himself and the great elements, self of action, victory, giver of action's fruit!"}},{"n":54,"text":"पादौ तव धरा देवी दिशो बाहुर्दिवं शिरः ।\nमूर्तिस्तेऽहं सुराः कायश्चन्द्रादित्यौ च चक्षुषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Earth is your feet, goddess; the directions your arms; heaven your head; I am your form; the gods your body; the moon and sun your eyes."}},{"n":55,"text":"बलं तपश्च सत्यं च धर्मः कामात्मजः प्रभो ।\nतेजोऽग्निः पवनः श्वास आपस्ते स्वेदसंभवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strength, austerity, truth and dharma born of desire, lord; fire is your brilliance, wind your breath, waters born of your sweat."}},{"n":56,"text":"अश्विनौ श्रवणौ नित्यं देवी जिह्वा सरस्वती ।\nवेदाः संस्कारनिष्ठा हि त्वयीदं जगदाश्रितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Ashvins are your ears forever, the goddess Sarasvati your tongue; the Vedas rest on your purifying rites; this whole world rests on you."}},{"n":57,"text":"न संख्यां न परीमाणं न तेजो न पराक्रमम् ।\nन बलं योगयोगीश जानीमस्ते न संभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We do not know your number, measure, brilliance, valor, strength, nor your origin, lord of yogis."}},{"n":58,"text":"त्वद्भक्तिनिरता देव नियमैस्त्वा समाहिताः ।\nअर्चयामः सदा विष्णो परमेशं महेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devoted to you, god, collected by our vows, we always worship you, Vishnu, the supreme lord, the great Lord."}},{"n":59,"text":"ऋषयो देवगन्धर्वा यक्षराक्षसपन्नगाः ।\nपिशाचा मानुषाश्चैव मृगपक्षिसरीसृपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sages, gods, gandharvas, yakshas, rakshasas, serpents, pishachas, humans, beasts, birds and reptiles,"}},{"n":60,"text":"एवमादि मया सृष्टं पृथिव्यां त्वत्प्रसादजम् ।\nपद्मनाभ विशालाक्ष कृष्ण दुःस्वप्ननाशन ॥","meaning":{"en":"and others of this kind have been created by me on earth through your grace, lotus-navel, wide-eyed Krishna, destroyer of bad dreams."}},{"n":61,"text":"त्वं गतिः सर्वभूतानां त्वं नेता त्वं जगन्मुखम् ।\nत्वत्प्रसादेन देवेश सुखिनो विबुधाः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the goal of all beings, you are their leader, you are the face of the world. By your grace, lord of gods, the gods are always happy."}},{"n":62,"text":"पृथिवी निर्भया देव त्वत्प्रसादात्सदाभवत् ।\nतस्माद्भव विशालाक्ष यदुवंशविवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your grace, god, the earth has always been free of fear. So be born, wide-eyed one, as the increaser of the Yadu line,"}},{"n":63,"text":"धर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय दैतेयानां वधाय च ।\nजगतो धारणार्थाय विज्ञाप्यं कुरु मे प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"for establishing dharma, for killing the Daityas, and for upholding the world. Grant my request, lord."}},{"n":64,"text":"यदेतत्परमं गुह्यं त्वत्प्रसादमयं विभो ।\nवासुदेव तदेतत्ते मयोद्गीतं यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This supreme secret, born of your grace, lord, Vasudeva: I have sung it to you exactly as it is."}},{"n":65,"text":"सृष्ट्वा संकर्षणं देवं स्वयमात्मानमात्मना ।\nकृष्ण त्वमात्मनास्राक्षीः प्रद्युम्नं चात्मसंभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having created the god Sankarshana, you yourself, Krishna, by yourself created Pradyumna, born of yourself."}},{"n":66,"text":"प्रद्युम्नाच्चानिरुद्धं त्वं यं विदुर्विष्णुमव्ययम् ।\nअनिरुद्धोऽसृजन्मां वै ब्रह्माणं लोकधारिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And from Pradyumna you created Aniruddha, whom they know as Vishnu, the imperishable. From Aniruddha I was created, Brahma, who upholds the worlds."}},{"n":67,"text":"वासुदेवमयः सोऽहं त्वयैवास्मि विनिर्मितः ।\nविभज्य भागशोऽऽत्मानं व्रज मानुषतां विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am made of Vasudeva, and was made by you alone. Dividing yourself into portions, go to the human state, lord."}},{"n":68,"text":"तत्रासुरवधं कृत्वा सर्वलोकसुखाय वै ।\nधर्मं स्थाप्य यशः प्राप्य योगं प्राप्स्यसि तत्त्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, having killed the asuras for the happiness of all the worlds, established dharma and won renown, you will in truth attain yoga."}},{"n":69,"text":"त्वां हि ब्रह्मर्षयो लोके देवाश्चामितविक्रम ।\nतैस्तैश्च नामभिर्भक्ता गायन्ति परमात्मकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For you, of immeasurable valor, the Brahma-sages and the gods in the world, as devotees, sing you by those many names as the Supreme Self."}},{"n":70,"text":"स्थिताश्च सर्वे त्वयि भूतसंघाः\nकृत्वाश्रयं त्वां वरदं सुबाहो ।\nअनादिमध्यान्तमपारयोगं\nलोकस्य सेतुं प्रवदन्ति विप्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All hosts of beings rest in you, taking refuge in you, giver of boons, strong-armed one. The brahmins call you without beginning, middle or end, of boundless yoga, the bridge of the world.\""}}]}]}